"<p>Nitrobase leverages <strong>Traefik v3</strong> to dynamically discover and route HTTP/HTTPS traffic to containers without restarting the proxy.</p>\n<h2>Automatic Free Domains (sslip.io)</h2>\n<p>For quick testing and development, Nitrobase automatically assigns free wildcard subdomains powered by <code>sslip.io</code>:</p>\n<pre class=\"shiki shiki-themes github-light github-dark\" style=\"--shiki-light:#24292e;--shiki-dark:#e1e4e8;--shiki-light-bg:#fff;--shiki-dark-bg:#24292e\" tabindex=\"0\"><code class=\"language-text\"><span class=\"line\"><span>https://app-123.192.168.1.100.sslip.io</span></span></code></pre>\n<h2>Adding Custom Domains</h2>\n<ol>\n<li>In your DNS provider (Cloudflare, Namecheap, Route 53), add an <strong>A record</strong> pointing your domain to the server's public IP.</li>\n<li>In Nitrobase, open your App, switch to the <strong>Domains</strong> tab, and enter your domain name (e.g. <code>api.example.com</code>).</li>\n<li>Click <strong>Save &#x26; Apply</strong>. Traefik immediately requests a free TLS certificate from Let's Encrypt via ACME HTTP-01 challenge.</li>\n</ol>"